+# Print-aware compact physical carrier implementation plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Build and falsify a text-preserving, print-aware compact session-message carrier against a nominal-area-matched legacy spatial-template baseline, without claiming the original 52,500-symbol Tardos threat model.
+
+**Architecture:** A small codec packs a 10-bit roster row and 22-bit synthetic session/message identifier with a 16-bit keyed check, then encodes the 48 bits as twelve extended-Hamming `(8,4,4)` blocks (96 codeword bits). The candidate carrier disperses seven analog repetitions across source-specific 32 px blank-region tiles and encodes each bit with equal-ink, complementary clustered-dot lobes; the baseline disperses fifty repetitions through the existing 12 px bipolar split template. A single runner copies the committed common source pack, generates the frozen observations and falsification controls, and writes finite JSON plus per-case CSV.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Python 3.11+, NumPy, Pillow, PyMuPDF, existing `nishan.tardos_carrier`, existing `nishan.registration`, `unittest`.
+
+**Spec:** `/tmp/sih-robustness-20260916-control/research/robustness_campaign/SPEC.md` and `research/robustness/physical_carrier/preregistration.json`.
+
+## Global constraints
+
+- Protected baseline is `f37e861dc02815adf1bebb3e1b45ff222dccf821`; all writes remain on `research/robustness-20260916-physical-carrier` in `/tmp/sih-robustness-20260916-physical-carrier`.
+- Use `__PRIVATE_CAPTURE_WORKSPACE__/SIH/.venv/bin/python` read-only with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; do not install dependencies.
+- Set `OMP_NUM_THREADS=2`, `OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=2`, and `MKL_NUM_THREADS=2`; target less than 1.5 GiB resident memory and 500 MiB added artifacts.
+- Historical `legacy-capture-0*.jpeg` captures are development-only channel diagnostics and are not evaluation data for this new carrier. New carrier evidence requires newly printed corresponding pages.
+- The 48-bit research message is not a UUID, deployment authenticator, content-binding proof, or collusion-equivalent fingerprint. The 16-bit keyed check does not justify a false-attribution security claim.
+- The roster has 1,000 rows, but the compact message has no collusion resistance. Exact whole-message recovery, ECC failures, tag failures, target-message mismatch, and abstentions are reported separately.
+- No more than two lead-specific physical-test PDFs may be selected: one candidate and one matched baseline. The coordinator's eventual pack must separately reference an unmarked source and original 52,500-symbol control.
+- Configuration, source allocation, transformations, metrics, and advancement rule are frozen in `preregistration.json` before evaluation.
+
+---
