+Each physical symbol uses one 32×32 blank tile, one of two complementary left/right or top/bottom lobes, sixteen 2×2 dark clusters (64 changed pixels), an 18-level neutral-luma decrement, and keyed orientation/polarity. Both bit values deposit the same number and strength of neutral-gray pixels. Select only tiles outside text boxes padded by 8 rendered pixels and with at least 99% of pixels at luma 254 or higher. Sum seven analog repetitions before the hard bit decision. Draw only the small opaque gray vector clusters in eligible blank tiles so PDF text objects remain unchanged and a page-wide transparency group cannot perturb text antialiasing.
