+# Compact print-aware physical carrier: frozen synthetic pilot
+
+Date: 2026-09-16
+Status: **synthetic advancement rule passed; physical robustness remains untested**
+
+## Decision
+
+The preregistered candidate `inkcluster_32_r7` advances to one fresh, matched physical falsification alongside `legacy_split_12_r50`. It recovered the entire expected 48-bit message in 30/36 positive synthetic cases versus 26/36 for the legacy comparator, and in 6/8 versus 5/8 confirmation-channel cases. All required clean, photo-resize, and halftone cases passed; every target-negative control avoided target acceptance.
+
+This is **not** evidence that the candidate is superior, invisible, physically robust, secure, or production-ready. Only nominal carrier area was matched. The candidate used a larger decrement (18 versus strength 4), source-informed blank allocation, fewer changed pixels, and substantially worse global PSNR (39.709 dB versus 46.204-46.250 dB). At inspection zoom its dots are plainly visible. No fresh print, camera, scanner, or WhatsApp observation was tested.
+
+## Hypothesis and frozen comparison
+
+The engineering hypothesis was that a 96-bit, ECC-protected session message placed as seven equal-ink clustered-dot repetitions in blank 32 px tiles would retain exact-message recovery through the frozen diagnostics while avoiding text pixels. It was compared with the existing 12 px split template carrying the same 96-bit word fifty times.
+
+| Property | Legacy comparator | Candidate |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Logical codeword | 96 bits | 96 bits |
+| Physical repetitions | 50 | 7 |
+| Physical symbols | 4,800 | 672 |
+| Block size | 12 px | 32 px |
+| Nominal area | 691,200 px | 688,128 px (-0.444%) |
+| Configured strength | 4 | 18-level luma decrement |
+| Placement | all keyed spatial blocks; text not avoided | source-specific tiles, padded text excluded, at least 99% luma >=254 |
+| Changed pixels/symbol | template-wide/clipped on white | 64 pixels in sixteen 2x2 clusters |
+| Coalition model | none in this compact comparison | none |
+
+This is nominal-area matching only. It is not matched measured distortion, local contrast, visibility, spatial freedom, embedding strength, or the original `m=52,500`, `c=5` threat model.
+
+The bounded message is `recipient_row[10] || synthetic_session_message_id[22] || keyed_check[16]` (48 payload bits) encoded as twelve independent extended-Hamming `(8,4,4)` blocks (96 coded bits). The target is row 7 and public synthetic message `0x2A1B3C`; row 29/message `0x155AA5` is the other-issued control. The 16-bit HMAC truncation is only a pilot rejection check, not a deployment authenticator or false-attribution guarantee.
+
+## Matrix and exact-message recovery
+
+Every cell reports complete expected-message recovery, not a partial score or a row-only match.
+
+| Profile | Split | clean | jpeg55 | photo resize/JPEG | print halftone | scanner contrast | scanner bilevel |
+|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| `legacy_split_12_r50` | development | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 1/2 | 0/2 |
+| `legacy_split_12_r50` | validation | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 0/2 | 0/2 |
+| `legacy_split_12_r50` | confirmation | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 1/2 | 0/2 |
+| `inkcluster_32_r7` | development | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 0/2 |
+| `inkcluster_32_r7` | validation | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 0/2 |
+| `inkcluster_32_r7` | confirmation | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 2/2 | 0/2 |
+
+`jpeg55` is only a same-size codec diagnostic. `photo_resize_jpeg` is a deterministic resize/recompression diagnostic. Neither is a WhatsApp result or physical-photo result. Synthetic registration was off; the read-only fresh-capture scorer forces content registration on.
+
