+
+## Negative and transplantation controls
+
+For each profile, all 18 unmarked observations, six wrong-key observations, and six wrong-context observations abstained. All six other-issued observations decoded the complete valid row-29 message but never accepted the expected row-7 message. Across both profiles, target acceptance was therefore 0/72 mandatory target-negative observations.
+
+All 12 copied-overlay/modified-content observations recovered the donor's complete row-7 message: 12/12 explicit content-binding failures. This is expected for a residual transplant and shows that message recovery does not establish document authenticity, ledger truth, who copied the pattern, or human culpability. Transplants were excluded from the target-negative gate exactly as preregistered, not hidden.
+
+## Fidelity and visibility
+
+Ranges span the six target PDFs; they are not confidence intervals.
+
+| Region/metric | Legacy comparator | Candidate |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Whole page PSNR | 46.204-46.250 dB | 39.709 dB |
+| Whole page MSE | 1.542-1.558 | 6.954 |
+| Whole page changed fraction | 17.653-20.718% | 2.146% |
+| Whole page max channel delta | 3 | 18 |
+| Text-region MSE | 1.525-1.540 | 0 |
+| Text-region changed fraction | 24.875-29.061% | 0% |
+| Text-region max channel delta | 3 | 0 |
+| Blank-region PSNR | 46.216-46.246 dB | 38.216-39.495 dB |
+| Blank-region changed fraction | 17.148-17.267% | 2.254-3.026% |
+| Blank-region max channel delta | 3 | 18 |
+| Extracted text identical | 6/6 | 6/6 |
+
+The candidate changed exactly 43,008 rendered pixels per page and none inside the unpadded text boxes. Its sparse marks are stronger, so global and blank-region PSNR are about 6.5-8.0 dB worse despite the lower changed fraction. The baseline's bipolar template clips asymmetrically against white paper and modifies many text pixels.
+
+The inspected 2x nearest-neighbor crop shows readable text in all panels, conspicuous candidate dot clusters, and lower-contrast diffuse baseline blocks. Poppler renders of both selected PDFs were one-page A4, unencrypted, with no clipping or layout overflow; the measured baseline text-pixel perturbation remains visible and disclosed. The inherited footer says “no watermark”; it is misleading on the marked derivatives, so the print operator must label sheets by filename. No blinded observer, print, or calibrated visibility study was performed.
+
+## Capacity and explicit failures
+
+Candidate eligible-tile counts were 929 (`dev_memo`), 727 (`dev_table`), 1,160 (`validation_dense`), 1,161 (`validation_diagram`), 1,679 (`test_short`), and 891 (`test_mixed`). This supports only 7-17 complete 96-bit repetitions. Frozen r7 fit every page, with `dev_table` at the seven-repetition floor.
+
+The fixed r18 probe required 1,728 tiles and was rejected on all 6/6 sources before embedding. The baseline had 13,860 total 12 px blocks on every page and needed 4,800. Capacity is therefore source-layout dependent and can fail on denser or differently formatted documents; the roster size does not imply carrier capacity.
+
+## Advancement-rule audit
+
+All frozen requirements passed without changing any seed, source, transform, profile, strength, threshold, or rule:
+
+- 12/12 clean positives recovered the entire expected message.
+- 0/72 mandatory target negatives accepted the expected message.
+- 12/12 target PDFs preserved extracted text.
+- 6/6 candidate PDFs had zero changed text-region pixels.
+- Candidate confirmation recovery was 6/8, not lower than the baseline's 5/8.
+- Candidate recovered both confirmation sources under both photo-resize/JPEG and print-halftone (4/4).
+
+Scanner-bilevel failures remained counted and disclosed. Passing this rule selects a page for a fresh physical falsification only.
+
+## Execution integrity and reproducibility
+
+The pre-evaluation implementation/configuration was committed as `ad4581f0798becd96e3a0253f11006f60415ea2c`; focused tests passed 22/22. Attempt 1 completed and wrote all 156 observation rows and arrays, then failed during packaging because `np.flatnonzero` was incorrectly unpacked as two coordinate arrays. Its manifest, CSV, arrays, and traceback are retained under `pilot_attempt1_packaging_failure/`.
+
+Only the post-evaluation visual-crop line was changed to `np.nonzero`; no algorithm, observation, transform, seed, threshold, or gate changed. Recovery attempt 2 ran from `67c2849d8116bc4d46107ec4e3c96e41b5ebebd1`. All 156 typed CSV outcome fields except runtime and both stored arrays were exactly equal between attempts. Attempt 2 completed in 147.194 seconds at 434,420 KiB peak RSS; final artifacts total 3,109,116 bytes. Final tests passed 26/26 after the read-only scorer and stricter frozen-identity/mask/ECC checks were added.
+
+- Configuration/preregistration SHA3-256: `6a97145dd1486aa9c77a79f809992e29cd26ee6eb83b2ae2b21ef96a445988ba`.
+- Runtime: Python 3.14.7; NumPy 2.5.3; Pillow 12.3.0; PyMuPDF 1.28.2; OpenCV headless 5.0.0.93.
+- Hardware: Intel Core i5-8350U, 4 cores/8 threads; Linux 7.2.4; OMP/OpenBLAS/MKL thread limits all 2.
+- Exact run and test commands: `pilot/command.log` and `pilot/test.log`.
+- Machine-readable retry comparison: `pilot/attempt_comparison.json`.
+- Full per-observation outcomes: `pilot/observations.csv`; full finite JSON and fidelity/capacity/control summaries: `pilot/results.json`; raw hard words/correlations: `pilot/observation_arrays.npz`.
+
+The prior 2026-09-12 compact pilot improved some synthetic BER but had no attribution-success-count improvement because its original comparator already succeeded everywhere; it had no physical test. This new pilot observes four additional candidate scanner-contrast recoveries overall, but the changed payload/threat model and much larger measured distortion prevent a same-threat or same-invisibility comparison. No published physical-document claim is treated as a measured comparator here.
+
+## Selected physical packet and next action
+
+The gate selected exactly two files:
+
+- `pilot/print_ready/test-mixed-candidate-row-7.pdf` - SHA-256 `2ec9016ab6de8bffbaa48b2e1efa81d69daa4b14dabeb52d59f7901c8ec21097`, SHA3-256 `a500a1b6351984d73d01b25ae22e4e45e1cf5172fa1818fff8e2a7d64dba4586`.
+- `pilot/print_ready/test-mixed-baseline-row-7.pdf` - SHA-256 `a642c6cf128b99405268faa150db6eaf57eb919b7c3dc35d2161d17b3e533ffa`, SHA3-256 `eacd3d268c570c371ce2c7e00f004d083cbeff483e2cc236784712028a6c9bae`.
+
+Print both at actual size with identical paper/printer settings. The eventual common packet must separately include/reference the unmarked `test_mixed.pdf` and coordinator-owned original 52,500-symbol control. Photograph every complete page upright under the same lighting/distance. Keep the original camera files and send them through WhatsApp **as documents**. If possible, obtain both a normal scanner capture and a separately labeled bilevel/binarized capture. Do not pool ordinary-camera, continuous-tone scanner, and bilevel results.
+
+Historical or newly supplied photos of an old carrier cannot validate these pages. Each score must use the matching source/profile. `score_capture.py` verifies the frozen hashes, forces content registration, and emits ECC corrections, uncorrectable blocks, full payload, tag validity, and exact-message match to stdout without writing into the pilot.
+
+The focused coordinator/GPT-6-Pro question is: **does the candidate's zero text-region distortion and 6/8 confirmation recovery justify this fresh print test despite its visibly stronger marks and roughly 6.5 dB worse whole-page PSNR, or should a separately named distortion-matched variant be preregistered before spending physical-test effort?** The current frozen rule answers only that the two-page falsification is worth trying.
+
+## Claim boundary
+
